Lip Dictation bundles and downloads third-party work:

- espnet/ — a trimmed copy of ESPnet (Apache License 2.0, Johns Hopkins University and ESPnet
  contributors) as distributed with "Visual Speech Recognition for Multiple Languages" by
  Pingchuan Ma et al. (github.com/mpc001/Visual_Speech_Recognition_for_Multiple_Languages).
  That repository's licence is in espnet/LICENSE-VSR. Local change: checkpoints are loaded with
  torch.load(weights_only=True).
- lipdictation/data/unigram5000_units.txt and 20words_mean_face.npy — from the same repository.
- Model weights (downloaded by scripts/download-models.sh, not stored in git): the Auto-AVSR
  LRS3 visual speech recognition model and subword language model by the same authors, and
  Google's MediaPipe face landmarker. The LRS3-trained weights are for research and private
  study only, not for commercial use.
- lipdictation/data/lexicon.tsv — common English words with their lip shapes and frequencies, made by
  scripts/make-lexicon.py from the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (Copyright 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon
  University, BSD-style licence, github.com/cmusphinx/cmudict) and word frequencies from wordfreq by
  Robyn Speer (data CC BY-SA 4.0, github.com/rspeer/wordfreq). This file is therefore shared under
  CC BY-SA 4.0.
- The on-device language model the app downloads is SmolLM2-360M by Hugging Face (Apache 2.0).
